window.PRINT_EVIDENCE = {"networks":[{"id":"hebrew","title":"Hebrew editions","intro":"Follow BHQ back to its manuscript base and its predecessors. Editorial succession and textual basis are different relationships.","nodes":[{"id":"ben","label":"Ben Hayyim","date":"1524/25","x":15,"y":15,"note":"A printed Masoretic text edited for Bomberg’s Second Rabbinic Bible."},{"id":"bh12","label":"BHK 1–2","date":"1906 / 1913","x":50,"y":15,"note":"Kittel used Ben Hayyim’s text, adding a critical apparatus."},{"id":"len","label":"Leningrad Codex","date":"1008/09","x":15,"y":52,"note":"A manuscript witness. The Society dates it 1008; 1008/09 is also used in cataloguing."},{"id":"bh3","label":"BHK 3","date":"1937","x":50,"y":52,"note":"Paul Kahle helped secure the change to a manuscript base."},{"id":"bhs","label":"BHS","date":"1967–77","x":83,"y":52,"note":"Elliger and Rudolph’s edition; Masorah work by Gérard E. Weil."},{"id":"bhq","label":"BHQ","date":"from 2004","x":67,"y":87,"note":"New apparatus and commentary, retaining Leningrad as base."}],"edges":[{"from":"ben","to":"bh12","label":"base text","type":"text","sourceIds":["bh-history"]},{"from":"bh12","to":"bh3","label":"series; base changes","type":"series","sourceIds":["bh-history"]},{"from":"len","to":"bh3","label":"base text","type":"text","sourceIds":["bh-history"]},{"from":"len","to":"bhs","label":"base text","type":"text","sourceIds":["bh-history"]},{"from":"bh3","to":"bhs","label":"editorial successor","type":"series","sourceIds":["bh-history"]},{"from":"bhs","to":"bhq","label":"editorial successor","type":"series","sourceIds":["bhq"]},{"from":"len","to":"bhq","label":"base text","type":"text","sourceIds":["bhq"]}],"defaultNode":"bhq","limit":"No direct copying line from Ben Hayyim to the Leningrad Codex is claimed. Ancient versions and additional Hebrew witnesses also inform the apparatus; they are not all drawn."},{"id":"early-greek","title":"Early Greek editions","intro":"Printed predecessors, manuscript variants and editorial revision meet. Select a node to see the precise relationships supported by the sources.","nodes":[{"id":"er","label":"Erasmus editions","date":"1516–1535","x":17,"y":16,"note":"Multiple editions, not one fixed text. The first two lack the Comma; the third includes it."},{"id":"cp","label":"Complutensian","date":"printed 1514","x":76,"y":16,"note":"Independent production at Alcalá; circulation later than its printing date."},{"id":"st","label":"Estienne / Stephanus","date":"1550","x":46,"y":49,"note":"An influential edition with marginal variants. The source account connects his work with Erasmus and the Complutensian."},{"id":"d","label":"Codex Bezae","date":"manuscript","x":85,"y":49,"note":"A Greek–Latin manuscript. Citing a reading does not mean adopting its entire text."},{"id":"be","label":"Beza’s editions","date":"later 16th c.","x":46,"y":85,"note":"Beza used textual variants collected by Robert and Henri Estienne."}],"edges":[{"from":"er","to":"st","label":"printed predecessor","type":"text","sourceIds":["dts"]},{"from":"cp","to":"st","label":"printed predecessor","type":"text","sourceIds":["dts"]},{"from":"d","to":"st","label":"variants in margin","type":"collation","sourceIds":["bezae"]},{"from":"st","to":"be","label":"Estienne collations used","type":"collation","sourceIds":["dts"]}],"defaultNode":"st","limit":"A selective evidence network, not a manuscript stemma. “Textus Receptus,” associated with the Elzevirs’ 1633 wording, names a printed tradition with differences, not a unique ancient manuscript."},{"id":"modern-greek","title":"Modern Greek editions","intro":"Nestle’s first edition combined published scholarship. Later editorial work returned to the witnesses and changed both the apparatus and the reading text.","nodes":[{"id":"ti","label":"Tischendorf","date":"19th-century edition","x":15,"y":15,"note":"One of the three editions compared by Eberhard Nestle."},{"id":"wh","label":"Westcott & Hort","date":"1881","x":50,"y":15,"note":"Another of Nestle’s three inputs, not the sole ancestor of the later edition."},{"id":"wy","label":"Weymouth","date":"19th-century edition","x":85,"y":15,"note":"Replaced by Bernhard Weiss’s edition in Nestle’s comparison in 1901."},{"id":"n","label":"Nestle","date":"1898","x":50,"y":48,"note":"Adopted the reading shared by two of his three edition inputs and recorded the alternative."},{"id":"ecm","label":"ECM","date":"research edition","x":15,"y":83,"note":"Extensive collations and editorial assessment, using CBGM for relevant work."},{"id":"na","label":"NA28","date":"2012","x":70,"y":83,"note":"A later member of a repeatedly revised series; ECM affected James–Jude here."}],"edges":[{"from":"ti","to":"n","label":"edition compared","type":"collation","sourceIds":["nestle"]},{"from":"wh","to":"n","label":"edition compared","type":"collation","sourceIds":["nestle"]},{"from":"wy","to":"n","label":"edition compared","type":"collation","sourceIds":["nestle"]},{"from":"n","to":"na","label":"series, intervening revisions","type":"series","sourceIds":["nestle"]},{"from":"ecm","to":"na","label":"Catholic Letters decisions","type":"text","sourceIds":["na28"]}],"defaultNode":"n","limit":"The gap from 1898 to 2012 contains substantial revision, not a direct reprint. Manuscript discoveries, collation and human judgment cannot be reduced to one ancestry line."}],"sources":[{"id":"getty","title":"Getty · The Making of a Medieval Book","url":"https://www.getty.edu/art/exhibitions/making/","type":"Museum exhibition","access":"Page read: parchment, ruling, copying, illumination and binding.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"materials","title":"Museum Plantin-Moretus · Printing Materials","url":"https://museumplantinmoretus.be/en/collection-research/de-collectie/printing-materials","type":"Holding museum’s technical account","access":"Page read: punches, cast type, type designers and typesetting. Applies to Plantin’s workshop, not a reconstruction of every detail of Gutenberg’s casting technique.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"workshop","title":"Museum Plantin-Moretus · The printing workshop","url":"https://museumplantinmoretus.be/en/seeing-doing/museum/printing-workshop","type":"Holding museum’s technical account","access":"Page read: composing, galleys, inking, impressions and proofreading. Production-rate claims not used.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"asia","title":"Library of Congress · Printing in Asia","url":"https://blogs.loc.gov/international-collections/2021/06/the-history-of-printing-in-asia-according-to-library-of-congress-asian-collections-part-1/","type":"Institutional history","access":"Search record reviewed; supports only the precedence of Asian printing and Bi Sheng’s movable type.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"gutenberg","title":"Library of Congress · Gutenberg Bible, volume 1","url":"https://www.loc.gov/resource/gdcwdl.wdl_04102_001/","type":"Digitized primary object and custodial description","access":"Catalogue/search record reviewed; full volume not read. Describes the Bavarian copy and its rubrication guide.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"cambridge","title":"Cambridge University Library · Great and Manifold Blessings","url":"https://wwwe.lib.cam.ac.uk/CUL/exhibitions/KJV/captions.html","type":"Institutional exhibition with shelfmarks","access":"Exhibition captions read, including Gutenberg, Erasmus, Luther, Tyndale, Coverdale, Geneva, Rheims and the KJV. Historical objects themselves not fully read.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"soncino","title":"Università Cattolica · The Soncino Hebrew Bible and Its Editions","url":"https://publicatt.unicatt.it/handle/10807/240477","type":"Research repository record","access":"Abstract and bibliographic record read; full chapter by Giancarlo Toloni (2023), pp. 58–78, not read.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"bh-history","title":"German Bible Society · History of Biblia Hebraica","url":"https://www.die-bibel.de/de/wissenschaftliche-ausgaben/biblia-hebraica/die-biblia-hebraica-von-rudolf-kittel-bhk/biblia-hebraica","type":"Publisher/editorial history","access":"Relevant historical sections read in German; dates and change of base text checked.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"bhq","title":"German Bible Society · Biblia Hebraica Quinta","url":"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/home/scholarly-editions/vulgate/scholarly-bible-editions/biblia-hebraica-quinta-bhq","type":"Edition project description","access":"Page read: diplomatic text, Masorah, apparatus and commentary. Not a reading of all fascicles.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"bomberg","title":"Museum of the Bible · Bomberg’s Miqra’ot Gedolot","url":"https://collections.museumofthebible.org/artifacts/44894-shaar-hashem-he-adash-daniel-bombergs-miqraot-gedolot?theme=collections-highlights","type":"Holding institution record","access":"Search record reviewed; dates 1525–26 differ from German Bible Society’s 1524/25. No individual-volume collation performed.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"complutensian","title":"Digital Complutensian · Chronology","url":"https://neelsmith.quarto.pub/digitalcomplutensian/complutensian/chronology/index.html","type":"Research project reporting primary colophons","access":"Chronology read. Direct colophon viewer failed. Uses explicit printing dates; warns that circulation in 1522 is inferred. Unrelated erroneous death-date sentence not adopted.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"eton","title":"Eton College · Complutensian Polyglot, B26443","url":"https://catalog.etoncollege.com/B26443","type":"Holding institution catalogue","access":"Search record reviewed; direct page fetch failed. Records Brocar, 1514–17 and qualified circulation circa 1522.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"newberry","title":"Newberry Library · Polyglots: Cathedrals of Print","url":"https://publications.newberry.org/polyglot/polylgot-text.pdf","type":"Institutional exhibition PDF","access":"Selected sections read: Complutensian layout/sources, named Hebrew editors, Latin aids and London subscription project. Not all bibliography read. Its Antwerp volume/language totals conflict with the holding museum; museum record preferred.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"plantin","title":"Museum Plantin-Moretus · The royal Bible in five languages","url":"https://museumplantinmoretus.be/en/royal-bible-five-languages-arias-montanus","type":"Holding institution","access":"Page read: Plantin, Montanus, Philip II, eight volumes and five languages.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"plantin-accounts","title":"Library of Congress / Plantin-Moretus · Royal Bible accounts","url":"https://www.loc.gov/resource/gdcwdl.wdl_11725/","type":"Digitized primary account book, 1568–78","access":"Catalogue/search record reviewed; ledger not transcribed. Record dates Bible production 1568–73.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"dts","title":"Dallas Theological Seminary Library · Some Rare Bibles","url":"https://digital.library.dts.edu/Pages/TL/Special/sc_bibles.shtml","type":"Institutional exhibition","access":"Search excerpts reviewed for Estienne and Beza; direct fetch timed out. Relation claims limited to those excerpts.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"bezae","title":"Cambridge · Digital recovery of a lost page of Codex Bezae","url":"https://specialcollections-blog.lib.cam.ac.uk/?p=15340","type":"Institutional research report","access":"Research account read in full on 2026-10-14; confirms Estienne 1550 marginal use of Codex Bezae. Underlying printed volume not independently collated.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"dejonge","title":"H. J. de Jonge · Erasmus and the Comma Johanneum (1980), pp. 381–389","url":"https://bibletranslation.ws/down/DeJonge-Comma-Johanneum.pdf","type":"Original research article; scan hosted by a third party","access":"Article pp. 381–389 read across two research passes, including conditional reply to Lee (385), Codex Britannicus discussion (386–387) and Bombasius correspondence. Original sixteenth-century replies/letters not independently inspected. Latin excerpt is quoted through this article.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"tregelles","title":"S. P. Tregelles · The Book of Revelation in Greek (1844), introduction","url":"https://assets.cambridge.org/97811080/07450/frontmatter/9781108007450_frontmatter.pdf","type":"Primary scholarly edition, Cambridge reprint excerpt","access":"Publisher description and indexed introduction excerpts reviewed; scanned-page retrieval failed. Full edition not read. Used only as further reading, not a sole authority for displayed relationships.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"mill","title":"R. C. Jebb · Bentley, chapter X: The proposed edition of the New Testament","url":"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/abs/bentley/proposed-edition-of-the-new-testament/A40E1B455D9078AC991CE847DF322D04","type":"Historical research, publisher chapter excerpt","access":"Excerpt located/reviewed: Mill’s 1707 edition and thirty years of collecting variants. Full chapter not read.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"nestle","title":"German Bible Society · The Nestle’s History","url":"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/the-nestles-history","type":"Publisher/editorial history","access":"Page read: 1898 edition comparison, Weymouth replaced by Weiss in 1901, 1927 apparatus, manuscript verification and 1979 revision.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"intf","title":"University of Münster, INTF · Nestle-Aland","url":"https://www.uni-muenster.de/INTF/forschung/nestle-aland/index.html","type":"Edition research institute","access":"Project page read.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"na28","title":"German Bible Society · The NA28","url":"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/the-na-28","type":"Publisher/editorial account","access":"Page read: ECM influence on Catholic Letters, apparatus changes and Jude 5 as an example. Full NA28 apparatus not reproduced.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"na29","title":"German Bible Society · Preview of NA29","url":"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/the-na-29","type":"Publisher development notice","access":"Page read on 2026-10-13; describes an edition in preparation. Future changes are plans, not a completed publication claim.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"cbgm","title":"University of Münster, INTF · Coherence-Based Genealogical Method","url":"https://www.uni-muenster.de/INTF/en/forschung/cbgm/index.html","type":"Primary methodology project","access":"Project account read; method combines textual judgments with relations among witnesses, not automatic recovery of an autograph.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"lxx","title":"German Bible Society · History of the Rahlfs Septuagint","url":"https://www.die-bibel.de/wissenschaftliche-ausgaben/septuaginta/zur-geschichte-der-septuaginta","type":"Publisher/editorial history","access":"Page read in German: compact edition 1935, Hanhart revision 2006 and relation to the larger Göttingen project.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"goettingen","title":"Göttingen Septuagint · Publications","url":"https://septuaginta.uni-goettingen.de/publications/septuaginta/","type":"Primary edition project bibliography","access":"Publication register reviewed, especially Genesis (Wevers 1974); individual volumes not read.","checked":"2026-10-13"},{"id":"erasmus-page","title":"Basel University Library · Erasmus, Novum Instrumentum (1516), printed p. 183","url":"https://www.e-rara.ch/bau_1/content/pageview/896099","type":"Digitized primary edition; UBH BibG B 3; DOI 10.3931/e-rara-2849","access":"Catalogue, IIIF manifest and page image inspected. Printed pp. 182–183 inspected; p. 183 is used here. Greek and Latin witness clauses, chapter V, signature q3 and catchword checked visually. Full volume not read. Public Domain Mark.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"agata","title":"Mari Agata · Stop-press Variants in the Gutenberg Bible, dissertation summary","url":"https://koara.lib.keio.ac.jp/xoonips/modules/xoonips/download.php/KO10001001-20062683-0002.pdf?file_id=132239","type":"Author’s Japanese dissertation summary, Keio repository","access":"Summary pp. 1–7 read, particularly digital comparison method and reported results. Reports 117 non-spacing changes on 88 pages; 277 including spacing on 216 pages. Nine digitized copies fully collated; wider checks involved 32 copies. These are study sample results, not all extant copies. Full dissertation retrieval failed; summary dated March 2006 internally, research profile lists degree work 2007. No page-level variant invented.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"agata-report","title":"Mari Agata · Stop-Press Variants: First Report of the Collation (2003)","url":"https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/abs/10.1086/pbsa.97.2.24296024","type":"Research article record, PBSA 97/2, 139–165","access":"Publisher metadata and citation trail read; full article not accessed. Located as foundational study, not used for uninspected variant details.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"copy-history","title":"Paul Needham / Cambridge · The Gutenberg Bible","url":"https://exhibitions.lib.cam.ac.uk/behindthescenes/2014/10/23/the-gutenberg-bible-paul-needham/","type":"Bibliographical research essay at the holding library","access":"Indexed excerpt reviewed; direct fetch failed. Identifies Cambridge copy as setting copy for Heinrich Eggestein’s third Latin Bible, completed late 1469 or early 1470. Corroborated by Cambridge exhibition catalogue; marks not independently collated.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"prinsloo","title":"Gert T. M. Prinsloo · Diplomatic or eclectic critical editions? (2022)","url":"https://www.scielo.org.za/scielo.php?pid=S0259-94222022000100074&script=sci_arttext","type":"Original research, HTS 78/1, a7813; DOI 10.4102/hts.v78i1.7813","access":"Sections on edition types, Habakkuk 3:1 and 3:9, and synoptic alternative read. Reports Elliger’s BHS 1970 and Gelston’s BHQ 2010 treatment. On-page Hebrew phrase is a normalized teaching excerpt; apparatus is paraphrased from his comparison, not presented as independently collated or copied from BHQ. His criticism of reconstruction is attributed, not treated as consensus.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"hbce","title":"SBL Press · The Hebrew Bible: A Critical Edition","url":"https://www.sbl-site.org/sbl-press/browse-books/the-hebrew-bible-a-critical-edition/","type":"Editorial programme by project/publisher","access":"Search-indexed project statement read: corrected archetype, multiple ancient editions, retroversion, commentary and criticisms. Direct fetch returned 403. No claim to have read full volumes or verified promised digital features.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"hobbins","title":"John F. Hobbins · Taking Stock of Biblia Hebraica Quinta","url":"https://www.afet.de/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/Hobbins_BHQ.pdf","type":"Scholarly review essay, pp. 37–56","access":"Opening sections and discussion of BHQ, HaKeter, and Oxford Hebrew Bible read. Historical publication schedule is not used as current status. Discussion shows why a diplomatic main text is compatible with critical evaluation in notes.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"weis","title":"Richard D. Weis · Biblia Hebraica Quinta and the Making of Critical Editions (2002)","url":"https://doi.org/10.15699/tc.7.2002.07","type":"Foundational methodological article, TC 7","access":"Bibliographic record and abstract located; full-text mirrors failed. Its classification of editions is discussed through Hobbins and Prinsloo, not claimed as a direct full-text reading.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"haketer","title":"Bar-Ilan University · Mikra’ot Gedolot HaKeter","url":"https://cris.biu.ac.il/en/organisations/mikraot-gedolot-haketer-marcos-and-adina-katz/","type":"Primary editorial project description","access":"Project account read: Menachem Cohen, Aleppo Codex basis, Masorah, targum and commentaries, print and digital forms. Promotional superlatives and unsourced error totals not adopted.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"mcdonald","title":"Grantley McDonald · Biblical Criticism in Early Modern Europe (2016)","url":"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/biblical-criticism-in-early-modern-europe/5EDB2B5936F8DD80A374B39C12594533","type":"Scholarly monograph, Cambridge University Press","access":"Publisher description and contents read. The book extends the Comma question into confessional and social history; full book not read. No detailed claims about its individual arguments asserted.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"basel-erasmus","title":"University of Basel · Erasmus: Novum Instrumentum and Comma Iohanneum","url":"https://tales.nmc.unibas.ch/en/erasmus-von-rotterdam-3/ein-text-der-texte-8/zeittafel-82","type":"University exhibition","access":"German account read for Latin translation aims and controversy; its blanket statement about all pre-1516 Greek witnesses is not adopted.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"kjv-preface","title":"The Translators to the Reader · 1611 preface, modernized transcription","url":"https://mail.bible-researcher.com/kjvpref.html","type":"Primary preface via transcription of Oxford 1833 reprint","access":"Section on diverse senses in margins read. Transcription modernizes spelling and presentation and omits patristic references. Used for the translators’ stated policy, not proof of uniform practice in every verse. No inference from unrelated authors cited elsewhere in the preface.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"peabody","title":"Harvard Peabody Museum · Literacy and the Printing Press","url":"https://peabody.harvard.edu/galleries/digging-veritas-literacy-and-printing-press","type":"Archaeological exhibition and collection account","access":"Page read, including 1979 type discovery, James Printer and John Sassamon. Does not establish that the excavated letter printed a Bible: museum associates it with the 1666 grammar’s preface. Its broad North American press priority claim is not adopted.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"eliot","title":"Bridwell Library · Eliot Bible, revised edition (1685)","url":"https://bridwell.omeka.net/exhibits/show/prothrobible/american/eliot","type":"Holding library catalogue, Prothro B-64","access":"Record read: first complete edition 1663, revised edition 1685, Job Nesutan’s translation assistance and James Printer’s composition/correction work. No full Massachusett text read.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"eliot-afterlife","title":"Library of Congress · Eliot’s Bible (2024)","url":"https://blogs.loc.gov/loc/2024/08/eliots-bible/","type":"Institutional collection essay","access":"Page read for missionary context and use of Bible and other records in Wôpanâak language reclamation. Its reference to Geneva as source differs from other accounts naming KJV; no exclusive source-text chain claimed here.","checked":"2026-10-14"},{"id":"eliot-census","title":"The Wôpanâak Bible · A Census","url":"https://eliotcensus.org/about/","type":"Research project description","access":"Project introduction located: census of 1661 NT, 1663 Bible and 1685 edition, building on Eames/Pilling. Individual census entries not audited.","checked":"2026-10-14"}],"caseStudies":[{"id":"copy-and-edition","question":"Can two copies of the same edition differ?","observed":"Agata’s image comparison detected changes within settings, including type orientation, spelling and punctuation.","inferred":"Ordering corrected and uncorrected states can reconstruct production, but a bound copy can mix states of different sheets.","teachingModel":"Existing PRNIT/PRINT setting exercise retained; fictional word expressly labelled. No historical Bible variant is simulated as real.","sourceIds":["agata","agata-report","workshop"],"limit":"Published summary examined; full collation tables not inspected."},{"id":"page-183","question":"What can a printed page establish?","object":"Basel UBH BibG B 3, Novum Instrumentum (1516), printed p. 183, IIIF canvas 896099.","observed":"Greek in left column, Latin in right. At 1 John 5:7–8 the list is spirit, water, blood without the heavenly witnesses clause. Chapter V appears in Latin margin; bottom has signature q3 and a catchword.","transcription":{"greek":"τὸ πνεῦμα, καὶ τὸ ὕδωρ καὶ τὸ αἷμα","english":"the spirit, and the water and the blood","method":"Short normalized Greek excerpt: abbreviations expanded, typography and punctuation normalized. English is a literal study rendering, not a complete verse translation."},"inferred":"The two columns belong to one editorial project and cannot be counted as two independent ancient manuscript votes.","limit":"1519/1522 states are supported by research; only 1516 page directly inspected here. Handwritten marginal note is not dated or attributed.","sourceIds":["erasmus-page","dejonge","basel-erasmus"]},{"id":"promise","question":"Does Erasmus’s reply promise a future insertion?","primaryLocator":"Responsio ad Annotationes Eduardi Lei (May 1520), Clericus IX, col. 275 BC, quoted by de Jonge p. 385.","excerpt":"Si mihi contigisset unum exemplar","rendering":"If a single copy had come into my hands","observed":"The quoted Latin uses an unreal past condition; the continuation explains what Erasmus would have done.","interpretation":"De Jonge challenges the promise anecdote and reads the reply as a defense of earlier editions. Theological pressure and publishing aims matter, but motives remain argued interpretations.","sourceIds":["dejonge","mcdonald"],"limit":"This is a quotation through modern research, not a direct examination of the 1520 printing. No claim that a codex was proved manufactured to force a promise."},{"id":"habakkuk","question":"Does a revised apparatus require a revised main text?","passage":"Habakkuk 3:1","excerpt":"לַחֲבַקּוּק הַנָּבִיא","rendering":"of Habakkuk the prophet","observed":"Prinsloo reports no BHS note at this phrase, but a BHQ note recording omission of “the prophet” in the Barberini Greek version.","interpretation":"A reader gains a comparison without losing the diplomatic base text. Absence of an apparatus entry does not prove universal agreement.","limit":"Normalized phrase and paraphrased comparison, not a facsimile or complete apparatus. No independent collation of Barberini or the two printed editions.","sourceIds":["prinsloo","bhq"]},{"id":"edition-policy","question":"What is the main text trying to represent?","positions":[{"name":"BHQ","aim":"Document Leningrad as a stable reference, critically evaluate variants in apparatus/commentary."},{"name":"HBCE","aim":"Reconstruct earliest inferable textual forms; separate columns where ancient editions differ."},{"name":"Synoptic proposal","aim":"Prinsloo argues for contextual comparison of witness texts so compact apparatuses do not conceal assumptions."}],"interpretation":"Different answers make different research tools. Diplomatic does not mean uncritical, and a reconstructed archetype does not mean an author’s autograph.","sourceIds":["bhq","hbce","prinsloo","hobbins"],"limit":"The reconstruction debate is substantial; the synoptic proposal is an attributed argument, not the replacement consensus."},{"id":"translation-and-labour","question":"Whose work disappears from a book’s familiar name?","observed":"Bridwell’s 1685 revised Eliot Bible record names Job Nesutan and James Printer; Peabody identifies Printer as Nipmuc and documents his typesetting.","interpretation":"Translation, composition and correction could overlap in one skilled person while remaining distinct tasks. Missionary publication and later Indigenous language reclamation give the same text different purposes.","limit":"No exact distribution of translated passages among collaborators reconstructed. No exclusive Geneva/KJV base asserted. Excavated type belongs to broader press history, not automatically to this Bible.","sourceIds":["eliot","peabody","eliot-afterlife"]}]};
